{"id": "EUVD-2026-76632", "enisaUuid": "4b688b7d-8d50-3699-92da-ee6a1f7db429", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nubifs: fix out-of-bounds read in signature length check\n\nubifs_sb_verify_signature() bounds the on-disk ubifs_sig_node->len field\nbefore handing the signature payload to verify_pkcs7_signature(), but the\ncheck has the wrong sign:\n\n\tif (le32_to_cpu(signode->len) > snod->len + sizeof(struct ubifs_sig_node))\n\nThe signature bytes start sizeof(struct ubifs_sig_node) (UBIFS_SIG_NODE_SZ,\n64 bytes) into the node, so the payload is at most\n\n\tsnod->len - sizeof(struct ubifs_sig_node)\n\nbytes long. Adding the header size instead of subtracting it accepts a\ndeclared length up to 2 * UBIFS_SIG_NODE_SZ larger than the node actually\nholds -- past the end of c->sbuf, which is vmalloc(c->leb_size).\nverify_pkcs7_signature() -> pkcs7_parse_message() -> asn1_ber_decoder()\nis then handed that inflated length and reads beyond the allocation while\nwalking the DER headers. The node length comes straight from the mounted\nimage, so a crafted signed UBIFS image reaches this via\nubifs_read_superblock() before the signature is cryptographically checked.\n\nsnod->len is guaranteed to be >= UBIFS_SIG_NODE_SZ by the node scanner\n(c->ranges[UBIFS_SIG_NODE].min_len == UBIFS_SIG_NODE_SZ), so the corrected\nsubtraction cannot underflow. Legitimately signed images are unaffected: a\ncorrect superblock never declares a signature longer than the node it is\nembedded in.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:33", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab7405bd86331cc2dbc8201699d4adc33bea75e7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11abc34698cb3172badf8aa12e623f1bac98bbd8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8cc3da72cf57acb4b77442ea8cec48425dff7c06", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37a9d25a563f5f9103282954ce573c4a61321e7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f76b79d6e42af20682495bccd22f72c7164b0018", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1dc246f98bb94233effa4fa3ec7bf84700bb7d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83e1aa9f5f906c9b1f4949d0521f0f950a159d96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/95d27c1708bb6e8823c8e7c623f9abc2a91bf4bf"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8388-259p-82vg", "CVE-2026-89720"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "044af3c3-5887-3ddc-9773-26e2f931fcb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "817aa094842dfc3a6b98c9582d4a647827f66201 <95d27c1708bb6e8823c8e7c623f9abc2a91bf4bf"}, {"id": "0577b7f1-8c65-34f5-ae38-9cb99e837b2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1231bfce-9f58-360f-9aa2-24ff77ac32c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "817aa094842dfc3a6b98c9582d4a647827f66201 <ab7405bd86331cc2dbc8201699d4adc33bea75e7"}, {"id": "169be3d9-4876-3360-87f5-a6c693eb6fc7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "4a9fb5e1-cdea-349d-8aa2-8425c0c920df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "752f2529-97dd-3c52-b474-6ce96010d556", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7841e93c-d874-356c-b312-3b7fc6026fb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "83326565-4df8-3933-a88e-877cc08b185d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}, {"id": "94d3ee37-65ca-3692-934b-3bcee5fddc4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "b81b5713-fbc5-3061-aa5f-2457b09677dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":